\f0\fs28\b Technical Specification Document\b0\fs22\par
\par
\b 1. INTRODUCTION\b0\par
This document outlines the technical specifications for the Document Processing Engine v2.0. The system is designed to handle multiple document formats with high fidelity conversion to structured Markdown output.\par
\par
\b 2. SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS\b0\par
\par
\b 2.1 Hardware Requirements\b0\par
\tab - Processor: 64-bit, 2 GHz or faster\par
\tab - Memory: 8 GB RAM minimum, 16 GB recommended\par
\tab - Storage: 2 GB available disk space\par
\par
\b 2.2 Software Requirements\b0\par
\tab - Operating System: Windows 10/11, Linux, or macOS\par
\tab - Python 3.10 or later\par
\tab - Tesseract OCR 5.x (optional, for fallback OCR)\par
\par
\b 3. ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW\b0\par
The engine follows a pipeline architecture with three main stages:\par
\par
\tab 1. Input parsing and format detection\par
\tab 2. Content extraction and structure analysis\par
\tab 3. Markdown assembly and output writing\par
\par
\f1\fs20 def convert(input_path, output_path):\par
\tab """Main conversion entry point."""\par
\tab engine = detect_engine(input_path)\par
\tab result = engine.extract(input_path)\par
\tab write_markdown(result, output_path)\par
\f0\fs22\par
\par
\b 4. CONCLUSION\b0\par
This specification provides the foundation for building a robust document conversion system that prioritizes accuracy and structure preservation.\par
